      "impact": "minor",
      "page_id": "01J0K0GDABNZ5YHF7DWB9QV4PC",
      "incident_updates": [
        {
          "id": "01KTS52RYYHX87AEYV1AKYVDB6",
          "body": "Open browser tabs with old logins to the Intercom app may be causing ongoing login/logout churn - closing old tabs or restarting web browser will prevent this from happening.",
          "created_at": "2026-06-10T16:15:38Z",
          "display_at": "2026-06-10T16:15:38Z",
          "incident_id": "01KTRTZFVZKRNTW66N1G5S8Z4M",
          "status": "resolved",
          "updated_at": "2026-06-10T16:15:38Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "01KTRTZFVZ1N87AKZ2EZ6BVMCP",
          "body": "Earlier today at 10:10 UTC many teammates were forced to logout and log back into Intercom. In a small number of cases, server side rate limiting impaired logging back in, causing login loops. We've resolved this issue as of 13:00 UTC. Apologies for any disruption.",
          "created_at": "2026-06-10T13:19:05Z",
          "display_at": "2026-06-10T13:19:05Z",
          "incident_id": "01KTRTZFVZKRNTW66N1G5S8Z4M",
          "status": "monitoring",
          "updated_at": "2026-06-10T13:19:05Z"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "01KQFN6VS6ARP1XBR1K1SBYY59",
      "name": "Investigating: Compromised version of intercom-client npm package and intercom-php ",
      "status": "resolved",
      "created_at": "2026-04-30T16:58:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-08T11:53:06Z",
      "resolved_at": "2026-06-08T11:53:06Z",
      "impact": "minor",
      "page_id": "01J0K0GDABNZ5YHF7DWB9QV4PC",
      "incident_updates": [
        {
          "id": "01KTKH8K9JVZZ882ME5YRVBEAB",
          "body": "**Resolved**\n\nWe're closing this incident. On April 30, 2026 an attacker published malicious versions of intercom-client (v7.0.4) and intercom-php (v5.0.2). Both were removed from distribution within hours of discovery. No evidence of unauthorized access to customer data or Intercom accounts was found.\n\nIf you installed intercom-client@7.0.4 or intercom-php@5.0.2 on April 30 and haven't already done so, we recommend rotating any credentials configured in that environment. All other versions of both packages are safe.\n\nWe kept the incident open out of an abundance of caution while we completed credential rotation, hardened our infrastructure, and monitored closely for any follow-on activity. We're now satisfied it's fully remediated.",
          "created_at": "2026-06-08T11:53:06Z",
          "display_at": "2026-06-08T11:53:06Z",
          "incident_id": "01KQFN6VS6ARP1XBR1K1SBYY59",
          "status": "resolved",
          "updated_at": "2026-06-08T11:53:06Z"
        },
